{"answerable": true, "quotes": [{"source": "S2", "quote": "the contractor shall be entitled to an extension of time equal to the period of every such suspension PLUS 25%"}, {"source": "S1", "quote": "exceeds thirty days, the contractor shall, in addition, be entitled to such compensation as the Engineer-in- Charge may consider reasonable in respect of salaries and/or wages"}, {"source": "S1", "quote": "adding thereto 2% to cover indirect expenses of the contractor provided the contractor submits his claim supported by details to the Engineer-in- Charge within fifteen days of the expiry of the period of 30 days."}], "answer": "Extra time: A suspension ordered for safety of the works is reason (c) in Clause 15(i), and it is not due to the contractor's default [S2]. Under Clause 15(ii)(a), you are entitled to an extension of time equal to the period of the suspension PLUS 25%. This applies to the item or group of items with a separate completion period of which the suspended work forms a part [S2]. For example, a 40-day suspension would give 40 + 25% of 40 (10) = 50 days. This example is my arithmetic, not a figure from the source.

Idle labour: Yes, but only if the total suspension period for that item or group of items exceeds thirty days [S1]. In that case you are entitled to compensation that the Engineer-in-Charge considers reasonable for salaries and/or wages paid to your employees and labour remaining idle at site during the suspension, plus 2% to cover indirect expenses [S1]. You must submit a claim supported by details to the Engineer-in-Charge within fifteen days of the expiry of the 30-day period [S1]. If the suspension is 30 days or less, the quoted text gives no such compensation.

Longer suspensions: If the suspension lasts more than three months at a time, Clause 15(iii) gives further rights. Because this suspension is for safety (reason (c)), those rights apply, since the exception covers only reason (a), contractor default. The contractor may serve a notice requiring permission to proceed. If permission is not granted within 15 days, the contractor may treat the suspension as an omission of that part (if only a part is affected) [S1]. The contractor must give written notice of this intention within 10 days of the expiry of that 15-day period [S1][S3].", "missing": "The text provided does not show the start of Clause 15(ii)(b) (it begins mid-sentence) or whether anything further limits the idle-labour compensation. The 25% extension and the compensation are stated in the quoted clauses only."}

{"answerable": true,
"quotes": [
{"source": "S1", "quote": "Mobilization advance not exceeding 10% of the tendered value may be given"},
{"source": "S1", "quote": "The mobilization advance in (ii) above bear simple interest at the rate of 10 percent per annum"},
{"source": "S2", "quote": "days inclusive, on the outstanding amount of advance."}
],
"answer": "Under Clause 10B of the CPWD General Conditions of Contract, the mobilization advance may be up to 10% of the tendered value. It is given only if the contractor asks for it in writing within one month of the order to commence the work. [S1] The Engineer-in-Charge may extend that period for the request if he considers the circumstances reasonable. [S2] The advance carries simple interest at 10 percent per annum. [S1] The interest is calculated from the date of payment to the date of recovery, both days inclusive, on the outstanding amount of the advance. [S1][S2]",
"missing": "This answer comes from the CPWD contract. It does not cover the Rajasthan PWD tender notice, and the question did not ask about that notice."}

{"answerable": true, "quotes": [{"source": "S3", "quote": "यदि संवेदक का नजदीकी रिश्तेदार (प्रथम रक्त सम्बन्धी व उनके पति/पत्नि) कार्य से सम्बन्धित वृत अथवा अधीनस्थ कार्यालय में खण्डीय लेखाकार अथवा सहायक अभियन्ता से लेकर अधीक्षण अभियन्ता स्तर का किसी भी स्तर पर पदस्थापित हो तो उसे कार्य पर नियुक्त करने पर प्रतिबन्ध रहेगा।"}, {"source": "S2", "quote": "contracts in which his near relative is posted as Divisional Accountant or as an officer in any capacity between the grades of the Superintending Engineer and Junior Engineer"}, {"source": "S1", "quote": "Any breach of this condition by the contractor would render him liable to be removed from the approved list of contractors of this Department."}], "answer": "Yes, there are restrictions. Which one applies depends on the document.

Rajasthan PWD tender notice: If the contractor's close relative (a first-degree blood relative or that relative's spouse) is posted at any level from Divisional/Sectional Accountant or Assistant Engineer up to Supervising Engineer in the department or subordinate office related to the work, the contractor is prohibited from being appointed to the work. The Hindi text says "नियुक्त करने पर प्रतिबन्ध रहेगा", meaning there will be a bar on appointing him to the work [S3].

CPWD contract (a separate, central-government contract; this is what it says, labelled as such): The contractor is not permitted to tender for works in the CPWD circle responsible for award and execution of contracts in which his near relative is posted as Divisional Accountant or as an officer in any capacity between the grades of Superintending Engineer and Junior Engineer [S2]. Any breach can make the contractor liable to be removed from the approved list of contractors of the Department [S1]. If he is registered in another department, he is debarred from tendering in CPWD [S1]. "Near relatives" there means wife, husband, parents and grandparents, children and grand children, brothers and sisters, uncles, aunts and cousins and their corresponding in-laws [S1]. The CPWD contract also requires the contractor to give a list of gazetted and non-gazetted CPWD employees related to him [S5].", "missing": "The Rajasthan notice text does not say what penalty applies beyond the bar on appointment to the work. The Rajasthan text is from an OCR scan (it reads "वृत", which is probably a misreading), so its wording may be slightly imperfect."}

{"answerable": true, "quotes": [{"source": "S1", "quote": "ऑन लाइन निविदा में भाग लेने के लिए डिजिटल सर्टिफिकेट इनफोरमेशन टेक्नोलॉजी एक्ट – 2000 के तहत प्राप्त करना होगा"}, {"source": "S1", "quote": "निविदा दाता उपरोक्त डिजिटल सर्टिफिकेट सी सी ए (CCA) द्वारा स्वीकृत एजेन्सी से प्राप्त कर सकते है।"}, {"source": "S1", "quote": "जिन निविदा दाताओं के पास पूर्व में वैध डिजिटल सर्टिफिकेट हैं, नया डिजिटल सर्टिफिकेट लेने की आवश्यकता नहीं है।"}], "answer": "कानून: ऑनलाइन निविदा में भाग लेने के लिए डिजिटल सर्टिफिकेट इनफोरमेशन टेक्नोलॉजी एक्ट – 2000 (Information Technology Act, 2000) के तहत प्राप्त करना होगा। यह सर्टिफिकेट इलेक्ट्रोनिक निविदा पर हस्ताक्षर (साइन) करने के काम आएगा [S1]।

कहाँ से: निविदा दाता यह डिजिटल सर्टिफिकेट सी सी ए (CCA) द्वारा स्वीकृत एजेन्सी से प्राप्त कर सकते हैं [S1]।

अतिरिक्त: जिन निविदा दाताओं के पास पहले से वैध डिजिटल सर्टिफिकेट है, उन्हें नया सर्टिफिकेट लेने की आवश्यकता नहीं है [S1]। साथ ही निविदा प्रपत्र डिजिटल साइन के साथ ही प्रस्तुत करने होंगे, अन्यथा प्रस्ताव स्वीकार नहीं किए जाएंगे [S1]।", "missing": ""}
